# ── Textbook: never publish ──────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Huang, Pavement Analysis and Design (2004) is a copyrighted commercial text and
# this repository is PUBLIC. The 20 chapter/appendix PDFs were removed from here
# and purged from git history; the site cites the book and links to the UIUC
# Library instead. This rule exists so a future `cp Chapters/* public/textbook/`
# cannot quietly re-publish it. See src/data/release.ts.
public/textbook/

# Homework material is NOT ignored — it is released week by week, and unlocking a
# homework means copying that week's files from "Homeworks Fall 2024/" into
# public/homeworks/<id>/ and adding the id to RELEASED_HOMEWORKS. Copy only
# assignments, handouts and data: never solution keys (*_solutions*, *Key*),
# graded submissions, or exams — and check that a third-party handout is ours to
# redistribute before it goes in. src/data/release.test.mjs fails the build if a
# file is staged for a homework that is not released.

# ── Contact Stress Predictor: the trained model, never published ─────────────
# The phyContactGAN checkpoints (three x 135 MB), their 2.1 GB training arrays,
# and the offline pipeline that reads them. They are the authors' intellectual
# property (Lang, Villamil & Al-Qadi 2026, ICT) and this repository is PUBLIC.
# What the site ships is public/tools/contact-stress/ — a precomputed, 2 mm,
# PCA-compressed sample of the model's OUTPUT, plus the citation. Re-bake it
# with the scripts in "Contact Stress Predictor/pipeline/", never by copying a
# .pth anywhere near src/ or public/.
Contact Stress Predictor/
